  "notes": "Formed from {導|どう} (to lead, guide) + {電|でん} (electricity). Most often seen in the compound {導電性|どうでんせい} (electrical conductivity).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {導電|どうでん}{性|せい}: electrical conductivity\n- {導電|どうでん}{体|たい}: conductor (of electricity)\n- {導電|どうでん}{材料|ざいりょう}: conductive material\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {絶縁|ぜつえん}: insulation — the opposite property, blocking current\n- {通電|つうでん}: energizing — passing current through a circuit to power it",
